    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d297">

                <pb facs="0513" n="487" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg487"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">110.11 DU/3–3054</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d297-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1954-03-30">March 30,
                            1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Ambassador Makins asked me at Eden’s request how long I expected to be at
                    Geneva. I said I expected to be there only for the first week. The Ambassador
                    said he thought that Eden had hoped that
                    he and I might be there for a fortnight, so that “we might deal with the
                    Indochina matter”. I said I was very skeptical that Indochina would come up in a
                    serious way in the first fortnight; that I foresaw procedural difficulties in
                    this matter and was anxious myself, as I had indicated at Berlin, to get back
                    shortly.</p>
                <closer><signed>JFD</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
